From 5719827af80d11671c75eb2ce9d812488aecee5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:57:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 269/269] media: cec: meson: ao-cec-g12a: use the vendor
 rise_del_max on SM1

The SM1 CECB controller is set up with a CTRL2 rise_del_max of 2, the
value from the initial vendor bring-up. With some TVs connected every
transmit then fails at once with an initiator error, so the polls for a
logical address never reach the bus and no address can be claimed.

The vendor driver later raised this value to 0x15 because arbitration
was lost with other CEC devices on the bus, and then to 8 to pass CEC
CTS test 9.6.1. Use 8.

Fixes: aef5f47c9907 ("media: platform: meson-ao-cec-g12a: add support for SM1")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/cec/platform/meson/ao-cec-g12a.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/cec/platform/meson/ao-cec-g12a.c b/drivers/media/cec/platform/meson/ao-cec-g12a.c
index 02a2a3f7960e..3426c95ccf0b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/cec/platform/meson/ao-cec-g12a.c
+++ b/drivers/media/cec/platform/meson/ao-cec-g12a.c
@@ -616,7 +616,7 @@ static int meson_ao_cec_g12a_adap_enable(struct cec_adapter *adap, bool enable)
 
 	if (ao_cec->data->ctrl2_setup)
 		regmap_write(ao_cec->regmap_cec, CECB_CTRL2,
-			     FIELD_PREP(CECB_CTRL2_RISE_DEL_MAX, 2));
+			     FIELD_PREP(CECB_CTRL2_RISE_DEL_MAX, 8));
 
 	meson_ao_cec_g12a_irq_setup(ao_cec, true);
 
-- 
